Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [oe-core toolchain-version specific]

Under C23 (GCC 15's default -std=gnu23), an empty parameter list "()"
in a function declaration means "takes no parameters", not "unspecified
parameters" as under prior C standards. Two declarations in this tree
relied on the old K&R meaning and now conflict with how they're
actually called/declared elsewhere:

- gpu_callback_s.func is declared "void (*func)()" but its only call
  site passes one argument (c->cookie).
- vchiq_bulk_receive_handle's copy_pagelist parameter is defined as
  "int (*copy_pagelist)()" but vchiq_if.h's prototype for the same
  function already declares it with two arguments
  (char *, const struct pagelist_struct *), so the definition now
  conflicts with the header's declaration.

Give both their real signatures instead of the empty-parens shorthand.

diff --git a/interface/vchiq_arm/vchiq_lib.c b/interface/vchiq_arm/vchiq_lib.c
--- a/interface/vchiq_arm/vchiq_lib.c
+++ b/interface/vchiq_arm/vchiq_lib.c
@@ -537,7 +537,7 @@
    int size,
    void *userdata,
    VCHIQ_BULK_MODE_T mode,
-   int (*copy_pagelist)())
+   int (*copy_pagelist)(char *vcptr, const struct pagelist_struct *pagelist))
 {
    VCHIQ_SERVICE_T *service = find_service_by_handle(handle);
    VCHIQ_QUEUE_BULK_TRANSFER_T args;
diff --git a/interface/vmcs_host/vc_vchi_gpuserv.h b/interface/vmcs_host/vc_vchi_gpuserv.h
--- a/interface/vmcs_host/vc_vchi_gpuserv.h
+++ b/interface/vmcs_host/vc_vchi_gpuserv.h
@@ -58,7 +58,7 @@
 
 struct gpu_callback_s {
   // callback to call when complete (can be NULL)
-  void (*func)();
+  void (*func)(void *);
   void *cookie;
 };
 
